    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Define item values and weights.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nfunction knapsack01(\n  weights: readonly number[],\n  values: readonly number[],\n  capacity: number,\n): number {\n  const dp = new Array<number>(capacity + 1).fill(0);\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < weights.length; i++) {\n    const weight = weights[i]!;\n    const value = values[i]!;\n\n    for (let remaining = capacity; remaining >= weight; remaining--) {\n      dp[remaining] = Math.max(\n        dp[remaining]!,\n        dp[remaining - weight]! + value,\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  return dp[capacity]!;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction knapsack01Table(\n  weights: readonly number[],\n  values: readonly number[],\n  capacity: number,\n): number {\n  const dp = Array.from(\n    { length: weights.length + 1 },\n    () => new Array<number>(capacity + 1).fill(0),\n  );\n\n  for (let i = 1; i <= weights.length; i++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c <= capacity; c++) {\n      dp[i]![c] = dp[i - 1]![c]!;\n\n      const weight = weights[i - 1]!;\n      if (weight <= c) {\n        dp[i]![c] = Math.max(\n          dp[i]![c]!,\n          dp[i - 1]![c - weight]! + values[i - 1]!,\n        );\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return dp[weights.length]![capacity]!;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Example:\nweights=[1,3,4,5]\nvalues=[1,4,5,7]\ncapacity=7\nbest value = 9 using weights 3+4.\n\nStep 3 — Complexity:\nO(n × capacity) time.\n1D version O(capacity) space.\n\nCritical rule:\nFor 0/1 knapsack, iterate capacity downward in the compressed version. Upward iteration would allow an item to be reused.",
